hYjRhODIzY2VlZjVlMWEwM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/andresgoag/base_fullstack/commit/ec7fb6066420a8ad0ff46dec0b08f0ea132fe280","sha":"ec7fb6066420a8ad0ff46dec0b08f0ea132fe280","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andresgoag/base_fullstack/commits/ec7fb6066420a8ad0ff46dec0b08f0ea132fe280"}],"sha":"122d10eca955384688a8cdab4a823ceef5e1a03b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andresgoag/base_fullstack/commits/122d10eca955384688a8cdab4a823ceef5e1a03b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30700328?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andresgoag","id":30700328,"login":"andresgoag","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzAwMzI4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andresgoag","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andresgoag/base_fullstack/commits/ec7fb6066420a8ad0ff46dec0b08f0ea132fe280/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-08T16:47:40Z","email":"30700328+andresgoag@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Andres Gomez"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-08T16:47:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"andresgoag/feature/websocket-channels-sample (#22)\n\n* add implementation plan for websocket channels sample\n\n* Add Django Channels WebSocket echo sample with Redis channel layer\n\n- Add Redis service to docker-compose and wire backend dependency\n- Create websocket Django app with EchoConsumer: JWT first-message auth, group broadcast\n- Configure ASGI routing and channel layers in settings\n- Add useWebSocket hook and WebSocketDemo page with nav link\n- 7 new async consumer tests; all 17 backend tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address WebSocket channels code review feedback\n\n- Switch backend command to daphne for ASGI/WebSocket support\n- Fix asgi.py to initialize Django before importing routing (AppRegistryNotReady)\n- Fix consumer: add closing flag to prevent double-close race, guard channel_layer None on disconnect, send auth_ok on success, validate token presence before UntypedToken\n- Add URL regex anchor ^ to routing pattern\n- Restore --locked flag to uv sync in Dockerfile\n- Track isAuthenticated separately from socket open state in useWebSocket hook, null socketRef on cleanup\n- Use {id, text} message objects in WebSocketDemo to avoid index-as-key anti-pattern\n- Add WS_BASE_URL fallback in config.ts\n- Add CHANNEL_LAYERS_REDIS_URL to .env.sample\n- Replace test suite: use full ASGI app, add auth_ok assertion, add room isolation and oversized message tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address second-round code review feedback on WebSocket channels sample\n\n- Move message ID assignment into hook onmessage callback to avoid ref mutation during render\n- Add readyState guard before socket.close() in cleanup\n- Restructure onmessage to remove comment in useWebSocket hook\n- Use close code 4002 for oversized messages to distinguish from auth errors (4001)\n- Fix unique email+phone in valid_token fixture to prevent IntegrityError in async tests\n- Remove redundant @pytest.mark.asyncio decorators (asyncio_mode=auto handles this)\n- Make channel_layer_settings fixture explicitly yield for guaranteed cleanup\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* apply lint and format fixes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* small fixes\n\n* format\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"100ff7f131dcba87f2d53c9e1900784c3e06f170","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andresgoag/base_fullstack/git/trees/100ff7f131dcba87f2d53c9e1900784c3e06f170"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/andresgoag/base_fullstack/git/commits/ec7fb6066420a8ad0ff46dec0b08f0ea132fe280","verification":{"payload":"tree 100ff7f131dcba87f2d53c9e1900784c3e06f170\nparent b5c619e34cc1c94df46839bb6282e7b29045201b\nauthor Andres Gomez <30700328+andresgoag@users.noreply.github.com> 1778258860 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778258860 -0500\n\nandresgoag/feature/websocket-channels-sample (#22)\n\n* add implementation plan for websocket channels sample\n\n* Add Django Channels WebSocket echo sample with Redis channel layer\n\n- Add Redis service to docker-compose and wire backend dependency\n- Create websocket Django app with EchoConsumer: JWT first-message auth, group broadcast\n- Configure ASGI routing and channel layers in settings\n- Add useWebSocket hook and WebSocketDemo page with nav link\n- 7 new async consumer tests; all 17 backend tests pass\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address WebSocket channels code review feedback\n\n- Switch backend command to daphne for ASGI/WebSocket support\n- Fix asgi.py to initialize Django before importing routing (AppRegistryNotReady)\n- Fix consumer: add closing flag to prevent double-close race, guard channel_layer None on disconnect, send auth_ok on success, validate token presence before UntypedToken\n- Add URL regex anchor ^ to routing pattern\n- Restore --locked flag to uv sync in Dockerfile\n- Track isAuthenticated separately from socket open state in useWebSocket hook, null socketRef on cleanup\n- Use {id, text} message objects in WebSocketDemo to avoid index-as-key anti-pattern\n- Add WS_BASE_URL fallback in config.ts\n- Add CHANNEL_LAYERS_REDIS_URL to .env.sample\n- Replace test suite: use full ASGI app, add auth_ok assertion, add room isolation and oversized message tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Address second-round code review feedback on WebSocket channels sample\n\n- Move message ID assignment into hook onmessage callback to avoid ref mutation during render\n- Add readyState guard before socket.close() in cleanup\n- Restructure onmessage to remove comment in useWebSocket hook\n- Use close code 4002 for oversized messages to distinguish from auth errors (4001)\n- Fix unique email+phone in valid_token fixture to prevent IntegrityError in async tests\n- Remove redundant @pytest.mark.asyncio decorators (asyncio_mode=auto handles this)\n- Make channel_layer_settings fixture explicitly yield for guaranteed cleanup\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* apply lint and format fixes\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* small fixes\n\n* format\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/hOsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp64QAJWtDLEhcUDtPiwd6QyAAFOm\nx4vefwiI4ScUPt9O76iyO7N9MZMM7Vd8z8T2qrpgHK+B4B1Mj4jZiPZbh//yu+X9\nOmn5OHiN/D3j+b8H8vxB5wfsxsAoGQicdzC+wVBO3tZ8LbjC2j0E/+HQpaILqe8I\nGu7ufRxgGodH5Ol8lroZ4IavKWN2gRI18AbRDKxjmpQ5X1pYkEdfiUSkR1Tipy6I\nzjMVwVDvXo5xFlRd9J/0fwlEkHBPmBo3Yda26zeN++VSUgcOWsurNA1f5uZr2+CY\nhMt9qwtkYK0o+3VPh96uoxER/rJaRY8yTG/dCwXFZNZ/TW4yQWmsBrt9fhV7QF0u\nQvpDARQ7hotMiJV4/ttabhf4o1IkAHa475MZoL3mPlMaaVWUVp+dUfikGSqH9cAG\nXnrNhUZ4zid+L7wpo5YaoFzVnmsSY0ylrevygOt6agibuRwRkbyDgToCfE3Bc2VE\nJTBOcCOpgTvGj4phsV3lKtmp+8w3Q4hpOD0ClPF1lHyJt8OSMYY1WOx/2ixdy/5k\nMCYlHV3E3JDaEN9TElK1VQtED1aIc6upTjYg7NYMxUa483RjktcHXgpzksEI+Z1P\nuKHGA3S22i46LQ9Zc9TThOmX1LRPgx3aa9MyX2QfjLv1ZIQEy/mspuH95c3FS3oZ\ntoPnbynIKfM0qODpU2/W\n=NHFo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n